  "question": "Does an engine whose league approximations are set to documented 2020s league rates place the simulated total-runs distribution at the right level, without degrading its shape, on MLB games it has never seen?",
  "scope": {
    "covers": "the full-game simulation's total-runs DISTRIBUTION — its level (mean), its p10–p90 coverage and its PIT shape — which every game report prints as the median total and the p10–p90 line",
    "doesNotCover": "the over/under CALL. The dev study shows the call fails because the engine's game-to-game level barely follows the posted line (simulated mean rises 0.21 runs per line point where actual rises 1.32); no level mechanism repairs that, and the candidate's fixed-side P(over) stays far from calibrated on dev (ECE 0.167, log loss 0.76 vs coin 0.693). mlb_total stays PAUSED under the live-record gate whatever this test finds. A differentiation candidate (pitcher run prevention beyond strikeouts, park, lineup quality) is a separate future registration."
  },
